# ADR-2607198300: iut-lean — independent Lean 4 formalization of anabelian geometry / IUT under com-junkawasaki

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki
**Scope**: new repo `com-junkawasaki/iut-lean` (public); depends on the
ADR-2606302300 taxonomy amendment landed alongside this ADR.

## Context

The owner asked to start an independent, from-scratch Lean 4 formalization
project targeting anabelian geometry and inter-universal Teichmüller theory
(IUT) — Shinichi Mochizuki's claimed proof of the ABC conjecture — inspired
by, but not a fork of, the RIMS \"LANA\" initiative (a project associated
with Mochizuki, Johan Commelin, and Adam Topaz). Research prior to this ADR
confirmed LANA's official site, `anabelian.org`, is currently only a stub
with no public repository or code released, so there is no upstream to fork
from; this project is necessarily an independent, original effort built on
`mathlib4`.

Two placement decisions were made by the owner before this ADR was written
(recorded here, not re-litigated):

1. **Org**: `com-junkawasaki`, **public** visibility.
2. **Repo name**: `iut-lean` was tried first via `gh repo view` and found
   free, so it was used (the planned fallbacks, `iut-formalization` and
   `abc-iut-lean`, were not needed).

Placing this repo in `com-junkawasaki` required first correcting
ADR-2606302300 (org taxonomy, status `proposed` at the time — directly
amendable per the CLAUDE.md draft-amendment exception), whose org-taxonomy
table scoped `com-junkawasaki`'s end-state to \"cloud + data only\" following
the 2026-06-30 kotoba-lang `-clj` migration decision. That scope did not
account for Jun Kawasaki's personal/private research projects that are
neither cloud/data infrastructure nor a `kotoba-lang` library, `etzhayyim`
public-interest agent, or `gftdcojp` commercial product. The amendment
(applied as a separate commit immediately before this ADR) widens
`com-junkawasaki`'s end-state to \"cloud + data + Jun Kawasaki
personal/private research projects\" and records a dated Amendment section
in ADR-2606302300 itself, so `iut-lean` has a taxonomy-consistent home.

## Decision

1. **Create `com-junkawasaki/iut-lean`** (public) as a from-scratch Lean 4 +
   mathlib4 scaffold — no forked code, since LANA has published none.
2. **Scaffold contents** (original files, not copied from any LANA source):
   - `lakefile.lean` — package `iut-lean`, `require mathlib from git
     \"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4\"`, default target
     `lean_lib IutLean`.
   - `lean-toolchain` — pinned to the exact string fetched live from
     `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/master/lean-toolchain`
     at scaffold time (`leanprover/lean4:v4.33.0-rc1`), rather than a
     guessed version, so the project tracks whatever Lean version mathlib4
     currently requires. This pin will drift as mathlib4 advances; keeping
     it in sync is a manual follow-up, not automated by this ADR.
   - `IutLean/Basic.lean` — a single import-free placeholder file (one
     `decide`-checked arithmetic example) with no anabelian-geometry or IUT
     content yet, chosen so it can be type-checked without first resolving
     the `mathlib4` dependency via `lake update`.
   - `.gitignore` — Lean/Lake entries (`.lake/`, `build`, `.cache`,
     `.DS_Store`) sourced from mathlib4's own `.gitignore` rather than
     guessed.
   - `README.md` — states the project's purpose and goals, explicitly
     disclaims affiliation with or forking from LANA, and is honest that
     `lake update`/`lake build` have not been run or verified in this
     scaffolding pass.
3. **Build verification status**: neither `lake` nor `elan` were installed
   in the environment that created this scaffold (`which lake` / `which
   elan` both failed), so `lake update && lake build` was **not attempted**.
   This is recorded honestly rather than claimed as verified; getting a
   clean build (which requires fetching all of `mathlib4`, a very large
   repository) is an explicit follow-up.
4. **Manifest registration**: `orgs/com-junkawasaki/iut-lean` was added to
   `:manifest.repos/extra-projects` in `manifest/repos.edn`, and
   `manifest/west.yml` was regenerated for this single entry via
   `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry iut-lean` (minimal
   single-entry diff, not a wholesale regeneration), pinning to the pushed
   `main` HEAD of the new repo.

## Consequences

- `com-junkawasaki` now has an accepted taxonomy basis (via the
  ADR-2606302300 amendment) for personal/private research repos in addition
  to cloud+data infrastructure, so future similar projects do not need to
  force-fit into `kotoba-lang`/`etzhayyim`/`gftdcojp`.
- `iut-lean` currently contains zero mathematical content — this ADR
  records the decision to start and the scaffold shape, not any progress on
  anabelian geometry or IUT formalization itself.
- Follow-up work (not covered by this ADR): running `lake update`/`lake
  build` to verify the scaffold actually compiles against current mathlib4;
  choosing a license; beginning actual formalization content; monitoring
  `anabelian.org` in case LANA publishes code that this project may want to
  align terminology/scope with (with no obligation to do so, since this
  project is independent).

## Rejected alternatives

1. **Fork or vendor LANA's code.** Not possible — LANA has no public
   repository to fork; `anabelian.org` is a stub.
2. **Place the repo in `kotoba-lang` (library axis) or `gftdcojp`
   (commercial product axis).** Rejected — this is Jun Kawasaki's personal
   research project, not a language/infra library and not a commercial
   product; it fits the newly-amended `com-junkawasaki` personal-research
   scope instead.
3. **Guess a Lean toolchain version.** Rejected — mathlib4's required
   toolchain changes over time; the live-fetched `lean-toolchain` from
   mathlib4 `master` is authoritative and avoids a stale guess.

## References

- ADR-2606302300 (org taxonomy, 4 orgs) — amended alongside this ADR to
  widen `com-junkawasaki`'s scope.
- `orgs/com-junkawasaki/iut-lean` — the new repo (public,
  `https://github.com/com-junkawasaki/iut-lean`).
- `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/master/lean-toolchain`
  and `.../mathlib4/master/.gitignore` — fetched live at scaffold time for
  the toolchain pin and `.gitignore` entries respectively.")))
